<section class="columns">

<p>Working people&mdash;not the wealthy few&mdash;should have the power to run society and the economy to ensure that everyone can live a dignified life.</p>

<p>Our goal is to build working-class power to make real, material change to improve our lives. That means a society where everyone has quality housing, a living wage, good working conditions, free healthcare, and access to education, and a flourishing environment&mdash;where democracy is measured by the power people have over the conditions of their daily lives.</p> 

<Image src={RoseRight} alt="<#alt#>" style={{ float:"right", width: "50%", height: "auto", shapeOutside: `url(${RoseRight.src})`, shapeMargin: "0.5em", }} />

<p>That's what democratic socialism looks like, and that's what we're building in Bloomington.</p>

<p><a class="button" href="about">Learn more</a></p>

</section>

<Calendar />

<Projects />

<section class="columns">

<Image src={RoseLeft} alt="<#alt#>" style={{ float:"left", width: "50%", height: "auto", shapeOutside: `url(${RoseLeft.src})`, shapeMargin: "0.5em", }} />

<p>“For the first time in the world’s history a subject class has it in its own power to accomplish its own emancipation without an appeal to brute force.</p>

<p>This is the appeal which socialism makes to the workers of this nation and the world.</p>

<p>It invites them to seize political power in the name of the working class, and to legally write their own economic emancipation proclamation.</p>

<p>Under this invitation the nations of the earth, including our own, are seething with political revolt.</p>

<p>It is the sure precursor of mighty changes—political, social, and economic—throughout the world.”</p>

<p style="text-align:right">– Eugene V. Debs, 1912<br>Terra Haute, Indiana</p>


</section>

